## 2. OWASP Top‑10 Review & Recommendations

| OWASP # | Category | Current Issue / Risk | Recommendation | Code Example |
|---------|----------|----------------------|----------------|--------------|
| **A01 – Broken Access Control** | No auth at all – anyone can read `/users`. | Add authentication (e.g., JWT) and role‑based checks. | See **Auth middleware** below. |
| **A02 – Cryptographic Failures** | No encryption/HSTS; uses plain HTTP. | Enforce HTTPS (via a reverse proxy or `express-enforces-ssl`) and set HSTS header. | `app.use(require('helmet').hsts({ maxAge: 31536000 }));` |
| **A03 – Injection** | No DB queries now, but future code could be vulnerable. | Use parameterised queries/ORM and validate/sanitize any query parameters. | Use `express-validator` or `Joi`. |
| **A04 – Insecure Design** | No layered defenses (headers, rate‑limit, CSRF). | Adopt a “defense‑in‑depth” stack: Helmet, rate‑limit, CSRF, secure cookies. | See sections below. |
| **A05 – Security Misconfiguration** | Default Express config (trust proxy off, error stack exposed). | Harden Express settings: `trust proxy`, disable `x-powered‑by`, set `env` properly. | `app.disable('x-powered-by'); app.set('trust proxy', 1);` |
| **A06 – Vulnerable & Outdated Components** | No lockfile version pinning shown. | Run `npm audit` regularly; lock versions in `package-lock.json`. |
| **A07 – Identification & Authentication Failures** | Same as A01 – missing auth. | Add JWT or session‑based auth, rotate secrets, store them in env vars. |
| **A08 – Software & Data Integrity Failures** | No integrity verification of dependencies. | Use `npm ci` with a lockfile, optionally enable `npm audit` CI step. |
| **A09 – Logging & Monitoring Failures** | Only console log on startup; no request/ error logs. | Add structured request logging (e.g., `morgan` + `winston`) and centralized error handling. |
| **A10 – Server‑Side Request Forgery (SSRF)** | No outbound requests now, but future endpoints may fetch URLs. | Validate any URLs before fetching, use allow‑list, set request timeout. |

