| **Uncontrolled lifecycle** – rotating or revoking a secret requires a new file deployment and a restart of every instance. |
| **No audit trail** – you cannot see who accessed or changed a secret. |
| **Environment‑wide exposure** – any process on the host can read the same environment variables, potentially including malicious containers. |
| **Inconsistent across environments** – each host may have a different `.env` version, leading to “works on my machine” bugs. |

