| **Environment drift** | Different environments (dev, staging, prod) must each keep their own `.env` file; manual sync errors lead to mis‑configurations or secret leakage. |
| **Rotation difficulty** | Updating a secret requires editing a file and restarting the process; there is no audit trail or automated rotation. |
| **No access control** | Everyone who can read the file on disk (devs, CI runners, backup snapshots) can view the secrets, regardless of the principle of least privilege. |

